REQUIREMENTS
------------
1. Java JDK 11 or higher
   Download : https://adoptium.net
   Choose   : JDK 21, Windows x64

2. Apache Tomcat 10
   Download : https://tomcat.apache.org/download-10.cgi
   Choose   : Binary Distributions > Core > zip


HOW TO DEPLOY (Step by Step)
-----------------------------

STEP 1 -- Install Java JDK
   - Download JDK 21 from https://adoptium.net
   - Run the installer
   - Tick "Add to PATH" during installation
   - Verify: open CMD and type:  java -version

STEP 2 -- Install Apache Tomcat
   - Download Tomcat 10 zip from https://tomcat.apache.org/download-10.cgi
   - Extract the zip to C:\tomcat10
   - Your folder should look like:
       C:\tomcat10\bin\
       C:\tomcat10\webapps\
       C:\tomcat10\conf\

STEP 3 -- Deploy this project
   Option A -- Deploy as WAR (easiest):
     Copy  awadhi-dictionary.war  into  C:\tomcat10\webapps\
     Tomcat will auto-unpack it when started.

   Option B -- Deploy as folder:
     Copy the entire  awadhi-dictionary-web  folder into  C:\tomcat10\webapps\
     Rename it to  awadhi-dictionary

STEP 4 -- Start Tomcat
   Open CMD and run:
     cd C:\tomcat10\bin
     startup.bat

   Wait about 10 seconds for Tomcat to start.

STEP 5 -- Open in browser
   Go to:  http://localhost:8080/awadhi-dictionary/

   Your Awadhi Dictionary website is now live!


HOW TO RECOMPILE JAVA FILES (if you make changes)
--------------------------------------------------
Open CMD in the project root folder and run:

   javac -encoding UTF-8 -cp WEB-INF\classes WEB-INF\classes\students\LexiconReader.java
   javac -encoding UTF-8 -cp WEB-INF\classes WEB-INF\classes\students\LexiconSearch.java

Then restart Tomcat:
   cd C:\tomcat10\bin
   shutdown.bat
   startup.bat


FEATURES
--------
1. Search by Awadhi word     -- Devanagari input, starts-with + contains match
2. Search by Hindi meaning   -- Whole-word match in Hindi column
3. Search by English meaning -- Whole-word match (e.g. "water" finds water, not "waterfall")
4. Search All                -- Searches all three columns at once
5. Browse by first letter    -- 40 Devanagari alphabet buttons
6. Quick-word links          -- Common words on welcome page
7. Result highlighting       -- Matched text highlighted in saffron
8. Stats cards               -- Total words, with/without English
9. Responsive design         -- Works on mobile and desktop


DATA FILES
----------
awadhi-config.txt   Tab-separated metadata file
                    Keys: LEXICON_NAME, STUDENT_NAME, CENTER_NAME, etc.

awadhi-lexicon.txt  Tab-separated dictionary data
                    Format: Awadhi Word [TAB] Hindi Meaning [TAB] English Meaning
                    Entries: 2414 words


TROUBLESHOOTING
---------------
Problem : Page shows garbled text (????? or boxes)
Fix     : Make sure Tomcat is using UTF-8. Add to C:\tomcat10\conf\server.xml
          inside the <Connector port="8080"> tag:
          URIEncoding="UTF-8"

Problem : 404 Not Found
Fix     : Check the URL is exactly http://localhost:8080/awadhi-dictionary/
          Make sure the folder/war name is awadhi-dictionary (no spaces)

Problem : Class not found error
Fix     : Recompile the Java files (see HOW TO RECOMPILE section above)

Problem : Port 8080 already in use
Fix     : Change port in C:\tomcat10\conf\server.xml
          Find: <Connector port="8080"
          Change to: <Connector port="8081"
          Then access at: http://localhost:8081/awadhi-dictionary/

